{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "F34_a_unit_the_registry_lacks_cannot_be_scaled",
    "description": "F34: the `units` registry is a CLOSED list and offers no way to scale an entry, so a quantity whose unit is not in the list cannot be declared honestly.\n\nWHAT THIS DOCUMENT WANTS. `County.barometricPressure` in MOVES is in INCHES OF MERCURY, and every expression that reads it multiplies by 3.38639 to reach kilopascals (docs/meteorology-generator.md 2.5). Declaring `units: \"inHg\"` on the variable that holds it is the whole point of a units field: it is what makes the 3.38639 a conversion rather than a magic number, and what would catch a document that divided by it instead.\n\nWHAT HAPPENS. `esm validate` refuses the document with `Unit string 'inHg' is not a recognised unit`. That refusal is correct given the registry -- esm-spec 1110's pressure row is `atm uatm bar hPa kPa mbar Torr mmHg psi`, a closed list, and `inHg` is not in it.\n\nWHAT MAKES IT A FINDING RATHER THAN A MISSING ENTRY. There is no escape hatch. Measured against the pinned toolchain, ALL of these are refused: `inHg`, `in`, `inch`, `in_i'Hg` (the UCUM spelling), `25.4 mmHg`, `25.4*mmHg`, `mmHg*25.4`, `inch*mmHg`. `mm` and `m` are accepted, so the registry has metric length and no imperial length, and a unit string carries no numeric scale factor. So the format can express millimetres of mercury and cannot express inches of mercury by ANY route, and a document holding one has exactly two options: declare a WRONG unit (`mmHg`, off by 25.4) or declare NO unit (`1`, which is what components/meteorology.esm does on its three pressure variables, with a sentence of prose in each `description` saying so).\n\nBoth options defeat the field. A wrong unit is worse than none, and a dimensionless declaration means the one arithmetic step this chain has that a dimensional check COULD catch -- multiplying inHg by 3.38639 to get kPa -- is unchecked.\n\nWHAT WOULD FIX IT, IN ORDER OF PREFERENCE. (a) A numeric scale factor in a unit string, so `25.4 mmHg` denotes what it says; that generalises past this case and past pressure. (b) Imperial length in the registry, so `inch` composes. (c) `inHg` as a registry entry, which fixes this document and nothing else. Any of the three turns this repro green.\n\nTHE ASSERTION BELOW IS THE INTENDED BEHAVIOUR, per docs/findings/README.md: the document loads, the variable holds 29.095, and its declared unit is the one it is in. It fails today at `esm validate`, before evaluation.",
    "authors": ["EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"],
    "tags": ["moves", "finding", "units", "meteorology"]
  },
  "index_sets": {
    "f34_county_rows": { "kind": "interval", "size": 1 }
  },
  "models": {
    "F34UnitScaling": {
      "tolerance": { "rel": 1e-12 },
      "variables": {
        "f34_barometricPressure": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": ["f34_county_rows"],
          "units": "inHg",
          "description": "`County.barometricPressure` for county 26161 (Washtenaw, Michigan), in inches of mercury -- the value fixtures/process-pm-exhaust.esm's zone reads through `Zone`. The `units` string is the finding."
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "_comment": "Washtenaw County's stored barometric pressure.",
          "lhs": "f34_barometricPressure",
          "rhs": { "op": "const", "args": [], "value": [29.095] }
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "a_pressure_in_inches_of_mercury_can_declare_its_unit",
          "description": "The intended behaviour: a document whose quantity is in inches of mercury declares that, loads, and evaluates. It fails at `esm validate` today -- `Unit string 'inHg' is not a recognised unit` -- so this assertion is never reached. If it is reached and passes, the registry has gained inches of mercury (or a scale factor, or imperial length) and components/meteorology.esm's three `units: \"1\"` pressure declarations, with their paragraph of apology each, should be replaced by the real unit.",
          "time_span": { "start": 0.0, "end": 0.0 },
          "assertions": [
            { "variable": "f34_barometricPressure", "time": 0.0, "expected": 29.095, "coords": { "f34_county_rows": 1 }, "tolerance": { "rel": 1e-12 } }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
